# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Env / secrets
.env
*.local

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Phase 2.5 archive-baseline WORKING output. `rows.jsonl` carries JD-derived evidence
# snippets for all 14,565 files — a bulk derived copy of a READ-ONLY archive that lives
# outside the repo (the `fixtures/golden/` precedent is for CURATED fixtures, not a dump).
# The audit trail that IS committed — `summary.json` + `errors.jsonl` — goes to
# `docs/baseline/`, written by the same run. Regenerate with `make baseline`.
/out/
# The default (machine-neutral) bind point for the archive, if a dev symlinks it in.
/archive/

# Fixtures may contain PII-scrubbed golden docs — tracked deliberately, so NOT ignored.

# Scratch files a test writes into the bind-mounted repo and cleans up after itself.
# Harmless on their own, but `git diff` hides untracked files, so a concurrent
# `git add -A` can sweep one into a commit — that has happened here before.
core/tests/fixtures/__scratch.*

# Claude Code local session state — never commit (accumulated permission grants)
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# GH-Copilot/ — the Copilot analysis inputs. The MARKDOWN is tracked (the triage
# record in docs/decisions/ cites it by path, so the citation must resolve); the
# generated explainer HTML, its `*_files/` asset directories and the zip bundles
# are ~2.5MB of derived output and are not.
GH-Copilot/*.html
GH-Copilot/*.zip
GH-Copilot/*_files/
